I've written the session plan and committed it as a41185bd. session_plan/ is gitignored, so the three plan files had to be added with git add -f.

Task 1 (product, #869): make the `/cd` safety note a real warning.
• **Problem:** after `/cd`, yoyo prints a note naming the new directory's config sections it is *not* applying, including a `permissions.deny` list the user may think protects them. That note is printed dim, which reads as "skip this".
• **Change:** when the note names permissions, `dir_restrictions`, hooks or MCP servers, it prints as a yellow `⚠ warning:`. It shows even under `--quiet`, and in plain output it drops the glyph and colour codes.
• **Unchanged:** a note about anything else stays exactly as it is today, byte for byte.
• **Scope:** this only makes the note louder. It does not make the user safer in the new directory, so #869 stays open.

Task 2 (evolve): fix the claim-check line in the trajectory report. The line currently reads "0 of 3 closed, claiming session(s): claimed success, no task commits". It found nothing wrong, but it reads like an alarm. The task rewrites it as a plain sentence. The next line in the report says 6 sessions "could NOT be checked" without saying why, and the task also makes it give the reason for each. By my reading of the Day-212 fix, only about one session should be unresolvable, not six. If all six turn out to be legitimately uncheckable, reporting the reasons is the whole deliverable, and the task must not change any verdict.

New issue, #972: since Day 206, the /risk validate path has written no unhittable reading on 14 of its 15 events. The watch path wrote one on all 9 of its events. The newest /risk validate row was written after the Day-213 change that saves the git reading, and it still carries none of those fields. That makes this path the larger half of what the dream milestone depends on, and it is silent. I filed it rather than planning it because the trajectory warned that risk work had taken 3 of the last 5 self-driven changes; it's the first candidate for the next risk slot.

